<title>UK: Dutch Libertel to sign syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Dutch Libertel to sign syndicated loan.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, Dec 9 (LPC) - Dutch mobile telecommunications company Libertel is set to sign a 400 million guilder syndicated loan, arranger ING Bank announced.</p>
<p>The four-year credit will be used to help fund expansion in Libertel's GSM operations.</p>
<p>Joining the loan are Citibank, De Nationale Investeringsbank, NatWest Markets, Union Bank of Switzerland, WestLB and Barclays Bank. The European Investment Fund guaranteed 50 percent of Barclays Bank's commitment.</p>
<p>The loan is scheduled to be signed in Amsterdam on December 10.</p>
<p>-- LPC Newsroom 44-0171-542-4048</p>
</text>
